<title>GERMANY: Waigel will not comment on details of reserve deal.</title>
<headline>Waigel will not comment on details of reserve deal.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG, Germany 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel declined on Thursday to comment on details of a compromise being worked out between the government and the Bundesbank regarding revaluation of central bank assets.</p>
<p>Asked repeatedly by reporters on the issue, Waigel said: &quot;I ask for your understanding,&quot; declining to make any comment.</p>
<p>&quot;We are having talks with the Bundesbank and only after that can a decision be reached on a change to the Bundesbank law,&quot; Waigel said.</p>
<p>He reiterated Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer's statement that talks between the two sides had been constructive.</p>
<p>-- Svea Herbst-Bayliss, Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
